Also check your dataValidator.sanitizeInput function (around line 950-960):

```javascript
sanitizeInput: function(input) {
    // Basic XSS protection
    if (typeof input === 'string') {
        return input
            .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
            .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
            .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
            .replace(/'/g, '&#x27;')
            .replace(/\//g, '&#x2F;');
    }
    return input;
},
```

This is likely the culprit! This function is converting characters like ' to &#x27; and / to &#x2F;, which is causing the & symbols you're seeing.

Replace it with this safer version:

```javascript
sanitizeInput: function(input) {
    // Basic XSS protection - but don't over-escape
    if (typeof input === 'string') {
        // Only escape the absolute minimum
        return input
            .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
            .replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
    }
    return input;
},
```

Or even better, create a new function specifically for display (not storage):

```javascript
sanitizeInput: function(input) {
    // For storage, we want raw data
    return input;
},

// For display only
escapeForDisplay: function(input) {
    if (typeof input === 'string') {
        return input
            .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
            .replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
    }
    return input;
},
```

